        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_988281955.1",
        "comments": "The assembly daVerOffc1.hap1.1 is based on 72x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Ancient Environmental Genomics Initiative for Sustainability (AEGIS,\nhttps://globe.ku.dk/research/ancient-environmental-genomics-initiative-for-sustainability). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using MitoHiFi and OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The genome was observed to be tetraploid (2n = 4x = 36). The chromosomes could not be confidently separated into distinct haplotypes or subgenomes and have therefore been submitted together as a whole genome. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on are uncertain on: Chromosome 1 (20,747 ? 33,892 Kbp), Chromosome 2 (29,782 ? 30,200 Kbp), Chromosome 6 (46,936 ? 49,110 Kbp), Chromosome 9 (11,760 ? 14,716, 23,746 ? 24,400 & 25,961 ? 26,924 kbp), Chromosome 11 (20,273 ? 23,690 Kbp), Chromosome 13 (26,868 ? 27,258 & 36,697 ? 37,682Kbp), Chromosome 14 (16,554 ? 17,057 Kbp), Chromosome 15 (20,346 ? 21,516 Kbp), Chromosome 16 (19,788 ? 22,353 Kbp), Chromosome 17 (17,038 ? 21,349 Kbp), Chromosome 20 (19,464 ? 24694 Kbp), Chromosome 21 (19,287 ? 21,795 Kbp), Chromosome 22 (17,791 ? 20,607 Kbp), Chromosome 23 (12,709 ? 13,712Kbp), Chromosome 29 (3,902 ? 5,407 Kbp), Chromosome 31 (11,260? 13,545 Kbp) & Chromosome 35 (11,817 ? 13,155 Kbp).",
